📍 Program 10 — File Pointer Navigation

📌 Description

This program demonstrates how to navigate through a file using file pointers.

It uses "tellg()", "tellp()", "seekg()", and "seekp()" to determine and change the current input and output positions in a file.

🔑 Concepts Covered

- 📍 File positions
- 🔎 Input-position navigation
- ✍️ Output-position navigation
- "tellg()"
- "tellp()"
- "seekg()"
- "seekp()"

📁 File Created

"navigation.txt"

🧠 Main Concept

Random navigation using file pointers
